{"book": "gate-da", "num": 5, "label": "5", "slug": "05-probability-statistics-mean-and-variance-of-a-random-variable", "title": "Mean and Variance of a Random Variable", "tag": "Probability & Statistics", "summary": "Let $X$ be a random variable with probability distribution $f(x)$. The expected value or mean of $X$ is defined differently based on whether $X$ is discrete or continuous:", "wordCount": 1212, "readingTimeMin": 6, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "5.1", "title": "Mean", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expected Value - Discrete and Continuous Cases", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with probability distribution $f(x)$. The <b>expected value</b> or <b>mean</b> of $X$ is defined differently based on whether $X$ is discrete or continuous:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Discrete case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu = \\mathbb{E}(X) = \\sum_x x f(x)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu = \\mathbb{E}(X) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x f(x) \\, dx"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example - Discrete Expected Value", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a discrete random variable with the following probability distribution:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|ccc}\nx & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n\nf(x) & 0.2 & 0.5 & 0.3 \\\\\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then the expected value is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}(X) = 1 \\cdot 0.2 + 2 \\cdot 0.5 + 3 \\cdot 0.3 = 0.2 + 1.0 + 0.9 = 2.1"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example - Continuous Expected Value", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the probability density function:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \n\\begin{cases}\n2x, & 0 < x < 1 \\\\\n0, & \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then the expected value is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}(X) = \\int_0^1 x \\cdot 2x \\, dx = \\int_0^1 2x^2 \\, dx = \\left[ \\frac{2x^3}{3} \\right]_0^1 = \\frac{2}{3}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expected Commission Calculation", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Problem:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "A salesperson for a medical device company has two appointments on a given day."}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "At the <b>first appointment</b>, there is a $70\\%$ chance ($P_1 = 0.7$) of making a deal with a commission of $1000."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "At the <b>second appointment</b>, there is a $40\\%$ chance ($P_2 = 0.4$) of making a deal with a commission of $1500."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The two appointments are independent."}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "What is the salesperson's <b>expected total commission</b> based on their own probability belief?"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Let $X_1$ be the random variable representing the commission from the first appointment, and $X_2$ for the second."}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbb{E}[X_1] &= (0.7)(1000) + (0.3)(0) = 700 \\\\\n\\mathbb{E}[X_2] &= (0.4)(1500) + (0.6)(0) = 600 \\\\\n\\text{Total Expected Commission} &= \\mathbb{E}[X_1] + \\mathbb{E}[X_2] = 700 + 600 = \\boxed{1300}\n\\end{align*}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "So, the expected commission is <b>$1300</b>."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expected Life of a Device", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Problem:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be the random variable that denotes the life in hours of a certain electronic\ndevice. The probability density function is"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n\\dfrac{20,000}{x^3}, & x > 100 \\\\\n0, & \\text{elsewhere}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Find the expected life of this type of device."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "The expected value (mean) of a continuous random variable $X$ with PDF $f(x)$ is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x f(x)\\,dx"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since $f(x) = 0$ outside $x > 100$, we compute:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_{100}^{\\infty} x \\cdot \\frac{20,000}{x^3} \\, dx \n= \\int_{100}^{\\infty} \\frac{20,000}{x^2} \\, dx"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Now compute the integral:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbb{E}[X] \n&= 20,000 \\int_{100}^{\\infty} x^{-2} \\, dx \\\\\n&= 20,000 \\left[ \\frac{x^{-1}}{-1} \\right]_{100}^{\\infty} \\\\\n&= 20,000 \\left[ 0 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{100} \\right) \\right] \\\\\n&= 20,000 \\cdot \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{200}\n\\end{aligned}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Answer:</b> The expected life of the device is <b>200 hours</b>."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expected Value of a Function of a Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with probability distribution $f(x)$. The expected\nvalue of the random variable $g(X)$ is given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\sum_x g(x) f(x) \\quad \\text{if } X \\text{ is discrete}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "and"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} g(x) f(x) \\, dx \\quad \\text{if } X \\text{ is continuous}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example: Expected Value of a Function of a Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Consider a random variable $X$ that denotes the number of cars arriving at a car wash in a day. The probability distribution of $X$ is:"}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/ps/fig016.png"], "caption": ""}, {"t": "p", "x": "Suppose the manager rewards the attendant according to the rule"}, {"t": "math", "x": "g(X) = 2X - 1,"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $g(X)$ represents the amount (in dollars) paid."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Task:</b> Compute the expected payment to the attendant during this one-hour period."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nThe expected reward is"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\sum_{x=4}^{9}(2x - 1)\\,P(X=x)."}, {"t": "math", "x": "= (7)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{12}\\right) + (9)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{12}\\right) + (11)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{4}\\right) + (13)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{4}\\right) + (15)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{6}\\right) + (17)\\left(\\tfrac{1}{6}\\right)."}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\tfrac{7+9}{12} + \\tfrac{11+13}{4} + \\tfrac{15+17}{6} \n= \\tfrac{16}{12} + \\tfrac{24}{4} + \\tfrac{32}{6}."}, {"t": "math", "x": "= 1.33 + 6 + 5.33 = \\boxed{\\$12.67}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus, on average, the attendant can expect to earn about $12.67 during this period."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example: Expected Value for a Continuous Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with density function"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \n\\begin{cases}\n\\frac{x^2}{3}, & -1 < x < 2 \\\\\n0, & \\text{elsewhere}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Let $g(X) = 4X + 3$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Find:</b> The expected value of $g(X)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>  we have:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\mathbb{E}(4X + 3) = \\int_{-1}^{2}(4x + 3)\\cdot \\frac{x^2}{3} \\, dx"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\frac{1}{3} \\int_{-1}^{2}(4x^3 + 3x^2) \\, dx = \\frac{1}{3} \\left[ x^4 + x^3 \\right]_{-1}^{2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Now compute:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\frac{1}{3} \\left[(2^4 + 2^3) - ((-1)^4 + (-1)^3)\\right] = \\frac{1}{3} \\left[(16 + 8) - (1 - 1)\\right] = \\frac{1}{3}(24) = \\boxed{8}"}]}]}, {"id": "5.2", "title": "Expectation of Joint and Marginal Distributions", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "<b>Expected Value of a Function of Two Random Variables</b>", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be random variables with joint probability distribution $f(x, y)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>1. Discrete Case:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "If $X$ and $Y$ are <b>discrete</b> random variables, and $g(X, Y)$ is a function of $X$ and $Y$, then the expected value (or mean) of $g(X, Y)$ is given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_{g(X,Y)} = E[g(X, Y)] = \\sum_x \\sum_y g(x, y) \\, f(x, y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>2. Continuous Case:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "If $X$ and $Y$ are <b>continuous</b> random variables, then the expected value is given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_{g(X,Y)} = E[g(X, Y)] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} g(x, y) \\, f(x, y) \\, dx \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Notes:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$f(x, y)$ is the joint probability mass function (PMF) for discrete variables or joint probability density function (PDF) for continuous variables."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$g(x, y)$ can be any function such as $x+y$, $xy$, $x^2 + y^2$, etc."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be the random variables with joint probability distribution indicated in table. Find the expected value of $g(X,Y)=XY$."}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|ccc|c}\nx\\backslash y & 0 & 1 & 2 & \\text{Row Totals} \\\\\n\n0 & 3/28 & 9/28 & 3/28 & 15/28 \\\\\n1 & 3/14 & 3/14 & 0 & 6/14? \\\\\n2 & 1/28 & 0 & 0 & 1/28 \\\\\n\n\\text{Column Totals} & 5/14 & 15/28 & 1/28 & 1\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n\nBy the definition of expected value:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY)=\\sum_{x}\\sum_{y} xy\\, f(x,y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Compute each term:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY)=(0\\cdot0)f(0,0) + (0\\cdot1)f(0,1) + (1\\cdot0)f(1,0) + (1\\cdot1)f(1,1) + (2\\cdot0)f(2,0)+\\cdots"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Only the term with $x=1$ and $y=1$ contributes:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = f(1,1) = \\frac{3}{14}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "<b>Example 2: Finding $E\\left(\\dfrac{Y}{X}\\right)$</b>", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Given:</b>\nJoint probability density function:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x, y) = \n\\begin{cases}\n\\dfrac{x(1 + 3y^2)}{4}, & 0 < x < 2,\\; 0 < y < 1 \\\\\n0, & \\text{elsewhere}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "We are asked to find the expected value:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E\\left(\\dfrac{Y}{X}\\right)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E\\left(\\dfrac{Y}{X}\\right) = \\int_0^1 \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{y}{x} \\cdot f(x, y) \\, dx \\, dy = \\int_0^1 \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{y}{x} \\cdot \\dfrac{x(1 + 3y^2)}{4} \\, dx \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Simplifying the integrand:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\int_0^1 \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{y(1 + 3y^2)}{4} \\, dx \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since the integrand is independent of $x$, integrate with respect to $x$ first:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\int_0^1 \\left[ \\dfrac{y(1 + 3y^2)}{4} \\cdot \\int_0^2 dx \\right] dy = \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{y(1 + 3y^2)}{4} \\cdot 2 \\, dy"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{y(1 + 3y^2)}{2} \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Expand and integrate:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "= \\int_0^1 \\left( \\dfrac{y}{2} + \\dfrac{3y^3}{2} \\right) dy = \\left[ \\dfrac{y^2}{4} + \\dfrac{3y^4}{8} \\right]_0^1 = \\dfrac{1}{4} + \\dfrac{3}{8} = \\dfrac{5}{8}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Final Answer:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E\\left(\\dfrac{Y}{X}\\right) = \\dfrac{5}{8}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expected Value from Joint and Marginal Distributions", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Note:</b> If $g(X, Y) = X$, then the expected value $E(X)$ can be calculated using either the joint or the marginal distribution:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Discrete Case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = \\sum_x \\sum_y x f(x, y) = \\sum_x x g(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $g(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X$, obtained by summing over all values of $y$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous Case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x f(x, y) \\, dy \\, dx = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x g(x) \\, dx"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $g(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x, y) \\, dy$ is the marginal density of $X$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Similarly, for $E(Y)$:</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Discrete Case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = \\sum_y \\sum_x y f(x, y) = \\sum_y y h(y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $h(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous Case:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y f(x, y) \\, dx \\, dy = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y h(y) \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $h(y) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x, y) \\, dx$ is the marginal density of $Y$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1: Discrete Random Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be discrete random variables with joint probability distribution given by:"}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/ps/fig017.png"], "caption": ""}, {"t": "p", "x": "Find $E(X)$ and $E(Y)$.\n\n<b>solution:</b>\n\nFirst, compute the marginal distributions:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Marginal of </b> $X$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P(X=0) = 0.1 + 0.2 + 0.1 = 0.4,\\quad P(X=1) = 0.1 + 0.2 + 0.1 = 0.4"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Marginal of </b> $Y$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P(Y=0) = 0.1 + 0.1 = 0.2,\\quad P(Y=1) = 0.2 + 0.2 = 0.4,\\quad P(Y=2) = 0.1 + 0.1 = 0.2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Now compute expectations:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Expected value of $X$</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = 0 \\cdot 0.4 + 1 \\cdot 0.6 = 0.6"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Expected value of $Y$</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = 0 \\cdot 0.2 + 1 \\cdot 0.4 + 2 \\cdot 0.4 = 1.2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion:</b> $E(X) = 0.6, \\quad E(Y) = 1.2$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2: Continuous Random Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with joint PDF:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x, y) = \n\\begin{cases}\n2, & 0 < x < 1,\\; 0 < y < 1 \\\\\n0, & \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Find the expected values $E(X)$ and $E(Y)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n\nThe joint PDF is uniform over the unit square."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Marginal of </b> $X$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "g(x) = \\int_0^1 f(x,y)\\,dy = \\int_0^1 2\\,dy = 2,\\quad 0 < x < 1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Marginal of </b> $Y$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "h(y) = \\int_0^1 f(x,y)\\,dx = \\int_0^1 2\\,dx = 2,\\quad 0 < y < 1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Expected value of $X$</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = \\int_0^1 x \\cdot 2\\,dx = 2 \\cdot \\left[ \\frac{x^2}{2} \\right]_0^1 = 1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Expected value of $Y$</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = \\int_0^1 y \\cdot 2\\,dy = 2 \\cdot \\left[ \\frac{y^2}{2} \\right]_0^1 = 1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion:</b> $E(X) = E(Y) = 1$"}]}]}, {"id": "5.3", "title": "Expectation of Conditional Probability Distribution", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expectation of Conditional Probability Distributions", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be random variables. The conditional expectation of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined as:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=y] = \\sum_x x\\, f(x\\mid y), \\quad \\text{(discrete)}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=y] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x\\, f(x\\mid y)\\, dx, \\quad \\text{(continuous)}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where the conditional probability/density is"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x\\mid y) = \\frac{f(x,y)}{h(y)}, \\quad f(y\\mid x) = \\frac{f(x,y)}{g(x)}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "and the marginals are denoted as"}, {"t": "math", "x": "g(x) = \\sum_y f(x,y) \\text{ or } \\int f(x,y) dy, \\quad \nh(y) = \\sum_x f(x,y) \\text{ or } \\int f(x,y) dx."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1 (Discrete)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ take values $1,2,3$ and $Y$ indicate group membership (0 or 1). Let the joint probability be $f(x,y)$. Find $E[X\\mid Y=1]$ and $E[X\\mid Y=0]$.\nCompute the marginals:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "h(y) = \\sum_x f(x,y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Conditional probabilities:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x\\mid y) = \\frac{f(x,y)}{h(y)}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then the conditional expectation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=y] = \\sum_x x \\, f(x\\mid y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Compute for $y=1$ and $y=0$ using the given table."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2 (Discrete)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Given joint PMF:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|cc}\nX\\backslash Y & 0 & 1 \\\\ \n0 & 0.2 & 0.1 \\\\\n1 & 0.3 & 0.4\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Find $E[X\\mid Y=0]$ and $E[X\\mid Y=1]$ using marginals $h(y)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n\nCompute marginals:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "h(0) = 0.2+0.3=0.5, \\quad h(1)=0.1+0.4=0.5"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Conditional PMFs:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x\\mid 0) = \\frac{f(x,0)}{h(0)} = \\{0.4,0.6\\}, \\quad f(x\\mid 1) = \\frac{f(x,1)}{h(1)} = \\{0.2,0.8\\}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Conditional expectations:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=0] = 0\\cdot0.4 + 1\\cdot0.6 = 0.6"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=1] = 0\\cdot0.2 + 1\\cdot0.8 = 0.8"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1 (Continuous)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ have joint density $f(x,y)=6x$ for $0<x<y<1$. Compute $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ using marginal $h(y)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n\nCompute marginal of $Y$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "h(y) = \\int_0^y f(x,y)\\, dx = \\int_0^y 6x\\, dx = 3y^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Conditional density:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x\\mid y) = \\frac{f(x,y)}{h(y)} = \\frac{6x}{3y^2} = \\frac{2x}{y^2}, \\quad 0<x<y"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Expectation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=y] = \\int_0^y x \\cdot f(x\\mid y)\\, dx = \\int_0^y x \\cdot \\frac{2x}{y^2} dx = \\frac{2y}{3}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2 (Continuous)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $f(x,y)=12 xy$ for $0<x<1,0<y<1$. Compute $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ using marginal $h(y)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n\nCompute marginal of $Y$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "h(y) = \\int_0^1 f(x,y)\\, dx = \\int_0^1 12xy\\, dx = 6y"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Conditional density:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x\\mid y) = \\frac{f(x,y)}{h(y)} = \\frac{12xy}{6y} = 2x, \\quad 0<x<1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Expectation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[X\\mid Y=y] = \\int_0^1 x\\cdot 2x\\, dx = \\frac{2}{3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Notice: $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ is independent of $y$."}]}]}, {"id": "5.4", "title": "Variance and Covariance", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Variance and Standard Deviation", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with probability distribution $f(x)$ and mean $\\mu$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Variance</b> of $X$ is given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2 = \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu)^2] = \\sum_x (x - \\mu)^2 f(x), \\quad \\text{if $X$ is discrete,}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2 = \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu)^2] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} (x - \\mu)^2 f(x)\\, dx, \\quad \\text{if $X$ is continuous.}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Standard Deviation</b> of $X$ is the positive square root of the variance:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Alternative Formula for Variance", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The variance of a random variable $X$ can also be computed using the formula:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2 = \\mathbb{E}(X^2) - \\mu^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\mathbb{E}(X^2)$ is the expected value of $X^2$,"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\mu = \\mathbb{E}(X)$ is the mean of $X$,"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\sigma^2$ is the variance of $X$."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Variance of a Function of a Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable and $g(X)$ be a function of $X$. Then the variance of $g(X)$ is given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}\\left([g(X) - \\mu_{g(X)}]^2\\right)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $\\mu_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}[g(X)]$ is the expected value of $g(X)$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Variance of a Transformed Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with probability distribution $f(x)$. The variance of the random variable $g(X)$ is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}\\left\\{[g(X) - \\mu_{g(X)}]^2\\right\\} = \\sum_x [g(x) - \\mu_{g(X)}]^2 f(x), \\quad \\text{if $X$ is discrete,}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}\\left\\{[g(X) - \\mu_{g(X)}]^2\\right\\} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} [g(x) - \\mu_{g(X)}]^2 f(x) \\, dx, \\quad \\text{if $X$ is continuous.}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1: Standard Deviation of Discrete Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a random variable with the following probability distribution:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|ccc}\nx & -2 & 3 & 5 \\\\\n\nf(x) & 0.3 & 0.2 & 0.5\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Compute the mean</b> $\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[X]$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu = (-2)(0.3) + 3(0.2) + 5(0.5) = -0.6 + 0.6 + 2.5 = 2.5"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Compute</b> $\\mathbb{E}[X^2]$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[X^2] = (-2)^2(0.3) + 3^2(0.2) + 5^2(0.5) = 4(0.3) + 9(0.2) + 25(0.5) = 1.2 + 1.8 + 12.5 = 15.5"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Compute variance and standard deviation</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2 = \\mathbb{E}[X^2] - \\mu^2 = 15.5 - (2.5)^2 = 15.5 - 6.25 = 9.25"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma = \\sqrt{9.25} \\approx 3.04"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2: Mean and Variance of Y = 3X - 2", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $Y = 3X - 2$, where $X$ has the density function:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \\begin{cases}\n\\frac{1}{4} e^{-x/4}, & x > 0 \\\\\n0, & \\text{elsewhere}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Mean and Variance of </b> $X$ (Exponential distribution)"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[X] = 4, \\quad \\text{Var}(X) = 4^2 = 16"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Use linear transformation rules</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[Y] = \\mathbb{E}[3X - 2] = 3 \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[X] - 2 = 3(4) - 2 = 10"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Var}(Y) = \\text{Var}(3X - 2) = 3^2 \\cdot \\text{Var}(X) = 9 \\cdot 16 = 144"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 3: Variance of g(X) = 3X<sup>2</sup> + 4", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Given:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \\begin{cases}\n\\frac{2(x+2)}{5}, & 0 < x < 1 \\\\\n0, & \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}\n\\quad \\text{and} \\quad g(X) = 3X^2 + 4"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Compute </b> $\\mu_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}[g(X)]$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\int_0^1 (3x^2 + 4) \\cdot \\frac{2(x+2)}{5} \\, dx"}, {"t": "p", "x": "First simplify the integrand:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "(3x^2 + 4)(2x + 4) = 6x^3 + 8x^2 + 24x + 32\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{5} (6x^3 + 8x^2 + 24x + 32)"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\mu_{g(X)} \n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\int_0^1 (6x^3 + 8x^2 + 24x + 32) \\, dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\left[ \\frac{6x^4}{4} + \\frac{8x^3}{3} + \\frac{24x^2}{2} + 32x \\right]_0^1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\left( \\frac{6}{4} + \\frac{8}{3} + 12 + 32 \\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\left(1.5 + 2.\\overline{6} + 12 + 32 \\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{48.\\overline{166}}{5} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{9.6334}\n\\end{aligned}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Compute </b> $\\mathbb{E}[g(X)^2]$ (use expansion of $g(X)^2 = (3x^2 + 4)^2 = 9x^4 + 24x^2 + 16$)"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbb{E}[g(X)^2] = \\int_0^1 (9x^4 + 24x^2 + 16) \\cdot \\frac{2(x+2)}{5} \\, dx\n\\quad \\text{(you can expand, integrate term-wise similarly)}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then compute:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma^2_{g(X)} = \\mathbb{E}[g(X)^2] - (\\mu_{g(X)})^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "(This step left as exercise for integration; numerical computation follows same idea.)"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Covariance of a Function of a Random Variable", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be random variables with joint probability distribution $f(x, y)$. The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ is"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_{XY} = E[(X - \\mu_X)(Y - \\mu_Y)] = \\sum_x \\sum_y (x - \\mu_X)(y - \\mu_Y) f(x, y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if $X$ and $Y$ are discrete, and"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_{XY} = E[(X - \\mu_X)(Y - \\mu_Y)] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} (x - \\mu_X)(y - \\mu_Y) f(x, y) \\, dx \\, dy"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if $X$ and $Y$ are continuous."}, {"t": "p", "x": "The covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ with means $\\mu_X$ and $\\mu_Y$, respectively, is also given by:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_{XY} = E(XY) - \\mu_X \\mu_Y"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1: Covariance of Discrete Random Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let the joint probability distribution of random variables $X$ and $Y$ be given as:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|cc}\nX \\backslash Y & 1 & 2 \\\\\n\n0 & 0.1 & 0.2 \\\\\n1 & 0.3 & 0.4 \\\\\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Find marginal probabilities</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P_X(0) = 0.1 + 0.2 = 0.3, \\quad P_X(1) = 0.3 + 0.4 = 0.7"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P_Y(1) = 0.1 + 0.3 = 0.4, \\quad P_Y(2) = 0.2 + 0.4 = 0.6"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Find means</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_X = 0 \\cdot 0.3 + 1 \\cdot 0.7 = 0.7"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_Y = 1 \\cdot 0.4 + 2 \\cdot 0.6 = 1.6"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Covariance formula</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathrm{Cov}(X, Y) = \\sum_x \\sum_y (x - \\mu_X)(y - \\mu_Y) f(x, y)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 4: Compute terms</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{aligned}\n(0 - 0.7)(1 - 1.6)(0.1) &= (-0.7)(-0.6)(0.1) = 0.042 \\\\\n(0 - 0.7)(2 - 1.6)(0.2) &= (-0.7)(0.4)(0.2) = -0.056 \\\\\n(1 - 0.7)(1 - 1.6)(0.3) &= (0.3)(-0.6)(0.3) = -0.054 \\\\\n(1 - 0.7)(2 - 1.6)(0.4) &= (0.3)(0.4)(0.4) = 0.048 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathrm{Cov}(X, Y) = 0.042 - 0.056 - 0.054 + 0.048 = -0.02"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Final Answer:</b> $\\boxed{\\mathrm{Cov}(X, Y) = -0.02}$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2: Covariance of Continuous Random Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with joint PDF:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x, y) = \n\\begin{cases}\n8xy, & 0 < x < 1, \\, 0 < y < 1 \\\\\n0, & \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Compute means</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_X = \\int_0^1 x \\left( \\int_0^1 8xy \\, dy \\right) dx = \\int_0^1 x \\cdot 4x \\, dx = 4 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\, dx = \\frac{4}{3}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_Y = \\int_0^1 y \\left( \\int_0^1 8xy \\, dx \\right) dy = \\int_0^1 y \\cdot 4y \\, dy = 4 \\int_0^1 y^2 \\, dy = \\frac{4}{3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Compute $E(XY)$</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = \\int_0^1 \\int_0^1 xy \\cdot 8xy \\, dx \\, dy = 8 \\int_0^1 \\int_0^1 x^2 y^2 \\, dx \\, dy = 8 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{8}{9}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Covariance</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathrm{Cov}(X, Y) = E(XY) - \\mu_X \\mu_Y = \\frac{8}{9} - \\left( \\frac{4}{3} \\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\right) = \\frac{8}{9} - \\frac{16}{9} = -\\frac{8}{9}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Final Answer:</b> $\\boxed{\\mathrm{Cov}(X, Y) = -\\frac{8}{9}}$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Correlation Coefficient", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be random variables with covariance $\\sigma_{XY}$ and standard deviations $\\sigma_X$ and $\\sigma_Y$, respectively. The correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y$ is defined as"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\rho_{XY} = \\frac{\\sigma_{XY}}{\\sigma_X \\sigma_Y}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 1: Covariance and Correlation (Discrete Case)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability distribution:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{array}{c|ccc}\nX \\backslash Y & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n\n1 & 0.1 & 0.1 & 0.2 \\\\\n2 & 0.1 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\\n\\end{array}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1:</b> Compute $E(X)$ and $E(Y)$."}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = 1(0.1 + 0.1 + 0.2) + 2(0.1 + 0.2 + 0.3) = 1(0.4) + 2(0.6) = 1.6"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = 1(0.1 + 0.1) + 2(0.1 + 0.2) + 3(0.2 + 0.3) = 0.2 + 0.6 + 1.5 = 2.3"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2:</b> Compute $E(XY)$."}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = 1\\cdot1\\cdot0.1 + 1\\cdot2\\cdot0.1 + 1\\cdot3\\cdot0.2 + 2\\cdot1\\cdot0.1 + 2\\cdot2\\cdot0.2 + 2\\cdot3\\cdot0.3\n= 0.1 + 0.2 + 0.6 + 0.2 + 0.8 + 1.8 = 3.7"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3:</b> Covariance"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Cov}(X, Y) = E(XY) - E(X)E(Y) = 3.7 - (1.6)(2.3) = 3.7 - 3.68 = 0.02"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 4:</b> Compute $\\sigma_X$ and $\\sigma_Y$."}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X^2) = 1^2(0.4) + 2^2(0.6) = 0.4 + 2.4 = 2.8 \\Rightarrow \\sigma_X^2 = 2.8 - 1.6^2 = 0.24\n\\Rightarrow \\sigma_X = \\sqrt{0.24}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{aligned}\nE(Y^2) &= 1^2(0.2) + 2^2(0.3) + 3^2(0.5) \\\\\n       &= 0.2 + 1.2 + 4.5 = 5.9 \\\\\n\\sigma_Y^2 &= E(Y^2) - (E(Y))^2 = 5.9 - 2.3^2 = 5.9 - 5.29 = 0.61 \\\\\n\\sigma_Y &= \\sqrt{0.61}\n\\end{aligned}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 5:</b> Correlation coefficient"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\rho_{XY} = \\frac{\\text{Cov}(X, Y)}{\\sigma_X \\sigma_Y} = \\frac{0.02}{\\sqrt{0.24}\\sqrt{0.61}} \\approx 0.052"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example 2: Covariance and Correlation (Continuous Case)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $f(x, y) = 4xy$ for $0 < x < 1$, $0 < y < 1$, and zero elsewhere. Let $X$ and $Y$ be random variables with this joint PDF."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1:</b> Compute $E(X)$, $E(Y)$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = \\int_0^1 \\int_0^1 x \\cdot 4xy \\,dy\\,dx = 4 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\left[\\int_0^1 y \\,dy\\right] dx = 4 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} dx = 2 \\int_0^1 x^2 dx = 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Similarly,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(Y) = \\frac{2}{3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2:</b> Compute $E(XY)$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = \\int_0^1 \\int_0^1 xy \\cdot 4xy \\,dy\\,dx = 4 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\left[\\int_0^1 y^2 \\,dy\\right] dx = 4 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} dx = \\frac{4}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{4}{9}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3:</b> Covariance"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Cov}(X, Y) = E(XY) - E(X)E(Y) = \\frac{4}{9} - \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{4}{9} - \\frac{4}{9} = 0"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 4:</b> Since covariance is zero, correlation is also zero:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\rho_{XY} = \\frac{\\text{Cov}(X, Y)}{\\sigma_X \\sigma_Y} = 0"}]}]}, {"id": "5.5", "title": "Linear Combinations of Expectation and Variance", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Linearity of Expectation", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $a$ and $b$ are constants, then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(aX + b) = aE(X) + b"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Setting $a = 0$, we get $E(b) = b$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Setting $b = 0$, we get $E(aX) = aE(X)$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example (Discrete)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ be a discrete random variable with $P(X = 1) = 0.3$, $P(X = 2) = 0.4$, $P(X = 3) = 0.3$.\nFind $E(2X + 3)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = 1(0.3) + 2(0.4) + 3(0.3) = 2.0 \\\\\nE(2X + 3) = 2E(X) + 3 = 2(2.0) + 3 = 7"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example (Continuous)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ have pdf $f(x) = 2x$ for $0 < x < 1$. Find $E(5X - 4)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = \\int_0^1 x \\cdot 2x \\, dx = \\int_0^1 2x^2 \\, dx = \\frac{2}{3} \\\\\nE(5X - 4) = 5E(X) - 4 = 5\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) - 4 = \\frac{10}{3} - 4 = -\\frac{2}{3}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expectation of Sum or Difference of Functions", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The expected value of the sum or difference of two functions of a random variable $X$ is the sum or difference of the expected values:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[g(X) \\pm h(X)] = E[g(X)] \\pm E[h(X)]"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example (Continuous)", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The weekly demand for a drink is $g(X) = X^2 + X - 2$, where $X$ has the density function:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \\begin{cases}\n2(x - 1), & 1 < x < 2 \\\\\n0, & \\text{elsewhere}\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nWe compute:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E[g(X)] = \\int_1^2 (x^2 + x - 2) \\cdot 2(x - 1) \\, dx"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Expand the integrand:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "(x^2 + x - 2)(2x - 2) = 2x^3 - 2x^2 + 2x^2 - 2x - 4x + 4 = 2x^3 - 6x + 4"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Now integrate:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\int_1^2 (2x^3 - 6x + 4) \\, dx = \\left[\\frac{2x^4}{4} - 3x^2 + 4x\\right]_1^2 \\\\\n= \\left[\\frac{2(16)}{4} - 3(4) + 8\\right] - \\left[\\frac{2(1)}{4} - 3(1) + 4\\right] \\\\\n= (8 - 12 + 8) - (0.5 - 3 + 4) = 4 - 1.5 = 2.5"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\boxed{E[g(X)] = 2.5}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Expectation of Product of Independent Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = E(X) \\cdot E(Y)"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be independent with:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = 2, \\quad E(Y) = 5"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(XY) = 2 \\cdot 5 = \\boxed{10}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Covariance of Independent Variables", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_{XY} = \\text{Cov}(X, Y) = E(XY) - E(X)E(Y) = 0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Example", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be independent random variables such that:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "E(X) = 1, \\quad E(Y) = 3, \\quad E(XY) = 3"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_{XY} = E(XY) - E(X)E(Y) = 3 - (1)(3) = 0"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\boxed{\\text{Cov}(X, Y) = 0}"}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b> Linear Combinations of Expectation and Variance</b>"}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/ps/fig018.png"], "caption": ""}]}]}], "sectionCount": 5}